Ladybird now takes the intrinsic widths of a replaced box from its
definite height through its aspect ratio wherever the box’s width is
a cyclic percentage. Run in Chrome 157.0.8103.79, Firefox 151.0, and
Playwright’s WebKit 26.5, all three engines make a flex container of
such an image 82.75px wide.

In Blink, ComputeMinAndMaxContentContributionForReplaced()
leaves unresolved a percentage width of an indefinite basis, so
ComputeReplacedSizeInternal() takes the inline size from the height
through InlineSizeFromAspectRatio(). In WebKit, RenderReplaced::
computeIntrinsicLogicalWidthContributions() doesn’t resolve percentage
widths, and computeAspectRatioAdjustedIntrinsicLogicalWidths()
multiplies the height by the ratio instead. In Gecko, nsLayoutUtils::
IntrinsicForAxis() replaces the contribution with the ratio-dependent
size of the definite height. All three compress a percentage width only
for the min-content contribution.
